            "review_title": "Review at Kim Long Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Tim C\nHong Kong215 contributions\n0\nAbsolutely Top Marks !\nSep 2016 • Friends\nOnce you manage to find this place in District 3, you will be in for a rare treat - cuisine from Royal Hue in a charmingly atmospheric restaurant. We ate a lot - snails, spring rolls, and many other exquisite dishes whose names I have forgotten already. Never mind, just look at the picture menu and order. If you have local friends, so much the better. \n\nThe young ladies who served us appeared a bit glum - I'm sure they are usually happy and smiling. Post-Independence Day holiday blues... perhaps. \n\nDo come here if you are spending time in Saigon. You might have to book - I'm not sure.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten September 4, 2016",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
