            "review_title": "Review at Kim Long Restaurant",
            "review_text": "thehiep\nAustin, Texas131 contributions\n0\nCentral Vietnam dishes at moderate prices\nJun 2012 • Couples\nThis restaurant offers dishes with flavor from Central Vietnam (\"Mon An Hue\"). It is located on a very narrow street, even by Vietnamese standard, and it is not easy to find. Its food is just average, but its prices are reasonable. Their service is also average, but the atmosphere is dismal, for lack of better words. The restaurant looks dated and is dark, and there is no A/C either. If you are unlucky as we were, having a table close by the restroom area, it is not pleasant! For a similar flavor of dishes, there are several better restaurants in District 1, close by Ben Thanh market. We will not recommend this one to our friends, and we do not plan to revisit either.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 27, 2012",
